Chapter: DeviceSeed

 device-seed reads the per-device entropy the identity key is derived
 from, so it carries Identity: the opening declares it, and the reads
 are act-bound rather than let-bound.

 Before that row existed this test declared only Console, the kernel
 gate denied every read, and all four words came back -1 — the same
 -1 an out-of-range index returns. The test passed on nothing but
 denials. It now tells the two apart: a valid index must not report
 the denial sentinel, and only index 4 may.

Section: Body
  seed-verdict : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  seed-verdict (s0) (s1) (s2) (s3) (bad) =
    if bad /= (0 - 1) then "FAIL: out-of-range not -1"
    else if s0 == (0 - 1) then "FAIL: word 0 denied"
    else if s1 == (0 - 1) then "FAIL: word 1 denied"
    else if s2 == (0 - 1) then "FAIL: word 2 denied"
    else if s3 == (0 - 1) then "FAIL: word 3 denied"
    else if s0 == 0 then if s1 == 0 then if s2 == 0 then if s3 == 0 then
      "FAIL: all zeros - RDRAND not working"
    else "PASS"
    else "PASS"
    else "PASS"
    else "PASS"

  opening : [Console, Identity] Nothing = act
    s0 <- device-seed 0
    s1 <- device-seed 1
    s2 <- device-seed 2
    s3 <- device-seed 3
    bad <- device-seed 4
    print-line-uni (seed-verdict s0 s1 s2 s3 bad)
  end
